Z||000000||87ECO5||03-14-2000||10:08 AM||||Anyone know the measurements of the seven bolts that hold the valve cover in place?  I know they require an 11mm socket.  What is the shaft length?  Are the threads a "standard" metric pattern?<P>Also, the two nuts that hold the filter canister lid in place ... I know they require a 13mm socket.  Do they also use a "standard" metric thread pattern?<P>MTIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||03-14-2000||06:54 PM||||All Fiero bolts are standardized metric hardware. Most sizes are commonly available at any autoparts and even many hardware stores. I belive metric bolt thread pitch is counted as threads per centimeter.<P>You can get a meteric bolt gauge & thread gauge just about as easy as SAE ones. Then you'll always know for sure what's in your hand.||||reg||1
